extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 2: Atlantis printed 17 (cache p017, a scan; page_offset 0). The entry begins under The Atlantean Nomad O.C.C. heading mid-page and ends at the foot of 17; printed 18 opens The Splugorth''s Atlantis. The Quick Find (printed 5) calls it Atlantean: Vagabond. Printed 17 was rendered; the OCR''s garble between Physical and Pilot is art, and nothing is missing. || XP: the Atlantean Vagabond ladder on printed 68, read off a render: lower bounds 0 / 1,901 / 3,601 / 7,201 / 14,401 / 24,501 / 35,001 / 45,001 / 65,001 / 85,001 / 115,001 / 145,001 / 185,001 / 250,001 / 310,001. || GROUP: optional, as the catalog''s vagabond, rogue-scholar and wilderness-scout; the book says the nomad is neither a practitioner of magic nor a warrior, so men_of_arms: false (heading True Atlantean Adventurer). || RACE: always a True Atlantean (the heading and ''possess all the special abilities and characteristics listed under the Atlantean R.C.C.''), so race_restrictions only true-atlantean, and the Marks of Heritage, racial S.D.C. and P.P.E. come from that race row and are not repeated here. || POOLS: no O.C.C. S.D.C. or P.P.E. is printed; the three extra tattoos add 10 S.D.C. and 6 P.P.E. each per the race''s rules (printed 16), stored as pool bonuses of 30 and 18. || TATTOOS: catalog spells, tradition tattoo. The Eye of Knowledge is fixed (Tattoo: Eye of Knowledge (language)); the other two are a starting group from a named list of the 32 tattoo rows less the three the character already holds (the Marks and the Eye). || SKILLS: Languages and Literacy Dragonese/Elf, American, Greek at 98% follow atlantean-monster-hunter exactly (Greek literacy as a Literacy: Other pick). Two languages +15% as two Language: Other picks. First Aid 45+10, Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+20, Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15, Lore: Faerie is Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic 25+10, Land Navigation 36+15, Wilderness Survival 30+15, Swimming 50+5. Hand to Hand prices one other skill for Expert and two for Martial Arts or Assassin (evil). || RELATED: seven, plus two at each of levels 3, 7, 11 and 15. Medical except Medical Doctor and cybernetics excludes Medical Doctor, M.D. in Cybernetics and Cybernetic Medicine. Espionage and Military none. Secondary: five from the same list without the bonuses. || MONEY: 2D6 x 1000 credits; the 4D6 x 1000 in gems or artifacts is salable goods, not coin, so it is prose. || EQUIPMENT: energy rifle as the catalog choice set other imports use; one W.P.-related weapon as weapons-matching-w-p-skills; rope as three 40 ft lengths; pocket tool kit as mini-tool-kit; the vehicle has no single catalog row and is prose."
---

## Lore

The Nomad is a True Atlantean with no single calling: a dimensional wilderness scout or an educated vagabond, trained broadly enough to survive wandering from world to world. Nomads have every ability of their race but are neither mages nor warriors, and they lean toward anarchist or unprincipled alignments.

Unlike most True Atlanteans they need, and often accumulate, real wealth, kept as cash or as possessions that are easy to sell, because a life always on the move means buying what they need where they are and never being weighed down by property or responsibility. A nomad earns money as a mercenary, laborer or scavenger.

Standard equipment: an energy rifle and one other weapon suited to the character''s W.P. skills, pocket and survival knives, a vibro-sabre, a cross, backpack, 1D4 sacks, utility belt, sleeping bag or tent, first-aid kit, sunglasses and goggles, air filter and gas mask, 100 ft of rope, a pocket tool kit, flashlight, and mega-damage environmental body armor such as the Bushman or Crusader. The vehicle can be any non-military ground vehicle suited to rough country, often a hover cycle, truck or robot horse.

Atlanteans avoid cybernetics: they are drawn to natural things and believe machinery weakens magic. A nomad who needs an implant seeks a bio-system.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'atlantean-nomad');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'atlantean-nomad';

